{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786993884,"nonce":"3e3vTFOi+CpiMXqlQcQ8tpx2+Vs=","title":"The roll-up's planner note reports missing indexes that migration 00021 wrote","message":"**What is wrong.** A measured planner note above `Rollup` says work is outstanding that is\nalready merged, and understates the query's plan on two of its three axes.\n\n**The demonstration.** `internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:810-813`:\n\n\u003e `namespace` and `fingerprint` have no (org_id, \u003ckey\u003e) index, so their keyset predicate is a\n\u003e filter rather than a range. They are still one grouped pass; the DDL that would make them\n\u003e index ranges is reported rather than written, because migrations are not owned here.\n\n`db/migrations/00021_rollup_indexes.sql` wrote that DDL:\n`CREATE INDEX alerts_ns_group_idx ON alerts (org_id, namespace)` at `:18-19` and\n`CREATE INDEX alerts_fp_group_idx ON alerts (org_id, source_fingerprint)` at `:23-24`. The\nmigration's own header at `:10-15` states the intent in the same words the comment says are\nunmet: \"These give the other two axes the same shape — a streaming GroupAggregate — and make\nthe roll-up keyset predicate an index range rather than a filter.\" The index comments at\n`:32-33` say the same again.\n\n**Why it matters.** This is a measured note, and a measured note is exactly the kind a reader\ntrusts without re-measuring. As written, the next person to tune this either re-writes an index\nthat already exists, or reads \"filter rather than a range\" and plans around a cost the database\nstopped paying at 00021. The repo's convention is that a comment claiming a measurement must\nstill be true; this one records a state of the world a migration ended.\n\n**Where.** `internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:799-813`;\n`db/migrations/00021_rollup_indexes.sql:10-24, 32-33`.\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** The note describes the current plan for all three axes, naming\n`alerts_ns_group_idx` and `alerts_fp_group_idx` the way it already names `alerts_name_idx`, and\nthe \"reported rather than written\" clause is gone. If the \"60 000 alerts, 280 ms versus 23 ms\"\nfigures were taken before 00021, the note says which axis they were measured on rather than\nimplying all three.","files":null}]}